# The acceptance truth table for the canonical ServiceRequest membership target, as CRE cases.
//
// ⚠ The PAUSE rows FAIL today, and that is the point — see `tests/serviceRequestTarget.test.ts`, which pins
// each lane's current shortfall beside the value it must reach. `result is` states what the case MUST
// produce; a `fail` here is the burn-down signal, never a case to re-author.
//
// ⭐ THE ROWS THAT MATTER ARE 2 AND 3, AND THEY MUST DIFFER. A request for some other service is a
// determinate NO — we looked at the request and it is not covered. No request at all is a question nobody
// has answered. `exists this` cannot tell them apart (both retrieve nothing); `matches this` can, because it
// reads the DATUM of a record that was actually retrieved.
//
// The stub code for a reference VS is `<canonicalBase>/CodeSystem/reference-vs-stub|<the VS canonical's last
// path segment>` — the SAME mechanical stub the FHIR ValueSet and the CQL retrieve use, so both lanes agree
// by construction. Here: canonicalBase `http://example.org/endoluminal-ablation`, VS `…/ValueSet/endoluminal-rfa`.
library "EndoluminalAblationCases".
covers "Endoluminal Ablation Coverage".

fact "Pat":
- name is "Pat".
- birth date is "1970-01-01".
- defined by "Patient".

// ── The RECORDED arm — a ServiceRequest, judged by the projection ──────────────────────────────
// A request carrying the covered code.
fact "RFA Request":
- code is "http://example.org/endoluminal-ablation/CodeSystem/reference-vs-stub|endoluminal-rfa".
- date is "2026-01-01".
- defined by "ServiceRequest".

// A REAL request for something else. ⭐ The row that separates this model from an `exists` one: the record
// exists and is retrievable, so the projection judges it and returns a determinate FALSE.
fact "Other Service Request":
- code is "http://example.org/endoluminal-ablation/CodeSystem/reference-vs-stub|some-other-procedure".
- date is "2026-01-01".
- defined by "ServiceRequest".

// ── The ASSERTED arm — a clinician answers the question directly ───────────────────────────────
fact "Answered Yes":
- value is true.
- date is "2026-02-01".
- defined by "Endoluminal Ablation Coverage"."Requested Service Is Endoluminal Radiofrequency Ablation".

fact "Answered No":
- value is false.
- date is "2026-02-01".
- defined by "Endoluminal Ablation Coverage"."Requested Service Is Endoluminal Radiofrequency Ablation".

// ── The truth table ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

case "request is the covered service -> approve":
- subject is "Pat".
- fact is "RFA Request".
- result is "Endoluminal Ablation Coverage" is "Approve Endoluminal Ablation".

// ⭐ A DETERMINATE false: the request was read and it is not the covered service.
case "request is a different service -> deny":
- subject is "Pat".
- fact is "Other Service Request".
- result is "Endoluminal Ablation Coverage" is "Deny Endoluminal Ablation".

// ⚠⚠ THE PAUSE ROWS ARE DELIBERATELY ABSENT FROM THIS FILE, AND THAT IS NOT AN OMISSION.
//
// CEL cannot say "no recommendation". `result is "<leaf>" is <branch | boolean>` is the whole surface
// (`cel/ast/types.ts`: `CELResultValue = CELBooleanResult | CELBranchResult`), so every case MUST name a
// branch. Writing the pause rows here would mean asserting a branch for a row whose correct answer is that
// NO branch fires — i.e. authoring the exact collapse this fixture exists to prevent, inside the oracle
// that is supposed to catch it.
//
// ⚠ That is not hypothetical: `fixtures/obesity/cases.cel` does exactly this today —
//   `case "obese unanswered -> no recommendation": - result is … is "Approve Bariatric Surgery".`
// — a case whose NAME says no recommendation and whose ASSERTION says Approve.
//
// ⚠ THIS IS A PERMANENT BOUNDARY, NOT A GAP TO CLOSE. CEL is Case EXAMPLE Language: a case exemplifies what
// a decision DOES, and you cannot exemplify an absence. There is no pause form and there will not be one —
// pause testing is what our tests are for.
//
// So the pause rows live where they can be stated truthfully: `MUST_PRODUCE` in
// `tests/serviceRequestTarget.test.ts` records them as `[]`, and `$apply` owns their EXECUTION. The two
// pause rows this fixture owes are:
//     no ServiceRequest at all              -> no recommendation
//     a ServiceRequest carrying NO code     -> no recommendation

// ── The asserted arm, and its recency merge with the recorded one ──────────────────────────────

case "answered yes, no request -> approve":
- subject is "Pat".
- fact is "Answered Yes".
- result is "Endoluminal Ablation Coverage" is "Approve Endoluminal Ablation".

case "answered no, no request -> deny":
- subject is "Pat".
- fact is "Answered No".
- result is "Endoluminal Ablation Coverage" is "Deny Endoluminal Ablation".

// ⭐ The merge: a NEWER assertion overrides an older record. The request says covered (2026-01-01); the
// clinician says no (2026-02-01); `most recent this` selects the assertion.
case "request covered but newer answer says no -> deny":
- subject is "Pat".
- fact is "RFA Request".
- fact is "Answered No".
- result is "Endoluminal Ablation Coverage" is "Deny Endoluminal Ablation".
